`, _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Signaling provides a highly efficient channel management mechanism for data transmission. Any user who subscribes or joins a channel can receive messages and events transmitted within 100 milliseconds. Signaling allows clients to subscribe to hundreds or even thousands of channels. Most Signaling APIs perform actions such as sending, receiving, and encrypting based on channels."
    }), `
`, _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Based on capabilities of Agora, Signaling channels are divided into two types to match different application use-cases:"
    }), `
`, _jsxs(_components.ul, {
      children: [`
`, _jsx(_components.li, {
        children: "Message Channel: Follows the industry-standard Pub/Sub (publish/subscribe) mode. You can send and receive messages within the channel by subscribing to a channel, and do not need to create the channel in advance. There is no limit to the number of publishers and subscribers in a channel."
      }), `
`, _jsx(_components.li, {
        children: "Stream Channel: Follows a concept similar to the observer pattern in the industry, where users need to create and join a channel before sending and receiving messages. You can create different topics in the channel, and messages are organized and managed through topics."
      }), `
`]
    }), `
